SUMMARY:2026 Pennsylvania Drum Show
DESCRIPTION:Sunday October 25th\, 2026\nEvent | 12:00 PM to 7:30 PM \nEarly Entry Access (12:00 PM – 7:30 PM) | $30 + Fees\nStandard Admission (1:00 PM – 7:30 PM) | $20 + Fees \nThis event is all ages – 21+ With Valid ID to Drink\nCome hungry! Snacks and light bites will be available at the canteen.\n————————————————–\nPresented by Drums Etc\n————————————————–\nThe Pennsylvania Drum Show is BACK for the Fall of 2026! This Marketplace\, Showcase and Community event draws drum enthusiasts from across America to celebrate everything drums & percussion! Started in 1995\, this is the 2nd longest running drum show in the country! Lancaster drum retailer\, Drums Etc. took the reins from Jack Lawton (Founder) back in 2023 and every year elevates the experience! This all-day event (12-7:30) takes place on the Rock Lititz Campus inside the premier music venue: Mickey’s Black Box. The  public is encouraged to pop-in or stay all day! \nAttendees will enjoy a massive indoor vendor Marketplace filled with New\, Used & Vintage drum gear\, try the latest gear from drum/cymbal manufactures in the “Industry Alley” section\, watch Educational Clinics by Gregg Bissonette [Ringo Starr All Star Band]\, Rob Mitzner [Author/Educator] & Fr. Hyacinth Cordell [Priest/Acclaimed Drummer]\, participate in Interactive Presentations (“Becoming a Durable Drummer” [Drummer Rx]\, Zildjian “Cymbal Talk”\, Drums Etc. Student Showcase\, Drum Circle [The Love Drums])\, have the opportunity to sell gear in the Consignment Marketplace (Item tags $5\, $20/set)\, and get to meet their heroes in the Meet & Greet Lounge (Tony Royster Jr [Katy Perry\, Jay-Z]\, Matt Greiner [August Burns Red]\, Jason Bittner [Shadows Fall] +more!). Every attendee receives a Raffle ticket with entry for a chance to win prizes donated by Drums Etc and industry supporters. Bar and concessions are available all day inside the MBB venue\, in addition to\, food vendors out front and on the Rock Lititz Campus. \nIn a conscious effort to give back to the local music scene\, Drums Etc. partnered with local businesses to elevate the 2026 show. A&E Audiology & Hearing Aid Center is co-sponsor for the event. Additionally\, presentations & clinics will take place on the “Keller Pro Audio Stage”\, attendees will buy/sell gear in the “Reason & Fritz Entertainment Consignment Market” and meet their heroes in the “SRCC Meet & Greet Lounge” (Susquehanna River Creative Conspiracy). \nThere are two ticketing options for the event. General Admission gains access to all clinics\, presentations and features throughout the day from 1-7:30pm. During this time\, attendees will have full access to the event marketplace\, in addition to the meet & greet lounge. VIP Early Access gains access 1 hour early to the event space (Noon-1). This is recommended for collectors looking for rare vintage pieces or attendees that wish to avoid large crowds. Kids under 10 years old are FREE! \nVisit the official show page here for full details & to register for booths! \nFor more information about the show\, booking information and a comprehensive list of VIP Artists attending the show visit Drums Etc. \nCONTACT: 717-394-3786 or Adam@DrumsEtc.com\n————————————————–\n*Ticket Alert* \nTickets for Mickey’s Black Box are sold through TicketMaster\, via our website\, or in person at our Box Office. Any tickets purchased elsewhere will not be honored and we are not responsible for tickets purchased from any 3rd party sellers. Do not google the name of the band to search for tickets. Go to Mickeysblackbox.com ONLY. Mickeysblackbox.com will never direct you anywhere but the official TicketMaster event site. \n\nAll bags are subject are to search upon entry. Tickets are non-refundable\, save for instances in which performances are cancelled by Mickey’s Black Box. For more information about our venue or to make an ADA request\, please visit the FAQ page of our website: https://mickeysblackbox.com/faq/ or call our box office line at (717) 723 – 8463.
URL:https://mickeysblackbox.com/event/2026-pennsylvania-drum-show/
LOCATION:Mickey’s Black Box\, 101 Rock Lititz Boulevard\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mickeysblackbox.com/app/uploads/2026/08/26-PADS-Banner-File-e1786712720501.jpg
END:VEVENT
